ore_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.16323612476125793,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.006221800998706728,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":28.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07154153566008041,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":90.6,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.019245150962150737,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":74.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004228782044953434,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00184,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.333,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":33.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Prudential Financial, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides financial products and services in the United States, Japan and internationally. It operates through PGIM, Retirement Strategies, Group Insurance, Individual Life, and International Businesses segments. The PGIM segment offers investment management services and solutions related to public fixed income, public equity, real estate debt and equity, private credit and other alternatives, and multi-asset class strategies to institutional and retail clients, as well as its insurance and retirement businesses. The Retirement Strategies segment provides a range of retirement investment, and income products and services to retirement plan sponsors in the public, private, and not-for-profit sectors; group annuities and other products; international reinsurance; investment only products; and FlexGuard suite, Fixed annuities, and variable annuities, as well as develops and distributes individual variable and fixed annuity products. The Group Insurance segment offers various group life, and long-term and short-term group disability, as well as group corporate-, bank-, and trust-owned life insurance; and supplemental health solutions including accident, critical illness, and hospital indemnity. The Individual Life segment develops and distributes variable life, universal life, and term life insurance products. The International Businesses segment develops and distributes life insurance, retirement products, investment products, and certain accident and health products. The company provides its products and services to individual and institutional customers through its proprietary and third-party distribution networks, financial professionals, and trusted partnerships. Prudential Financial, Inc. was founded in 1875 and is headquartered in Newark, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew Francis Sullivan | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 54 | Compensation: $6.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 36K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Prudential Financial, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $40.9B market cap on $60.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Management returns a meaningful 7.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 21% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 22% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.22223401187616373},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $43.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Prudential Financial Inc (PRU) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Japan Sales Suspension ...",